course: dictionary
lesson: 2120
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and «conversion» is one of them. The sentence around the word gives the clues that tell you which meaning fits. This is its context.
explain: In «In rugby union a try, worth 5, needs the ball pressed down on or over the opponents' goal line; a conversion adds 2», the words try, goal line and adds 2 show that a conversion is a kick in rugby. Swap in your meaning: "a kick at goal adds 2" still makes sense.
explain: In maths, the same word means something else. A conversion changes a measurement into different units, like centimetres to metres. So ask yourself: is this about sport, maths, a building or a belief? The answer shows you the meaning.
fact: A conversion means changing something from one form, unit or use to another.
fact: In maths, a conversion changes a measurement into different units, such as 1 km = 1000 m.
fact: In rugby, a conversion is a kick at goal after a try, worth two points.
fact: A loft conversion is a loft changed for a new use, such as a bedroom.
fact: Conversion can also mean a person changing their religion or coming to believe something.
exercise: «In rugby union a try, worth 5, needs the ball pressed down on or over the opponents' goal line; a conversion adds 2.» What does conversion mean here? | A person changing their religion | Changing centimetres into metres | A building changed for a new use | *A kick at goal after a try, worth two points
exercise: Maya says «1 kg = 1000 g» is a conversion. What does conversion mean in maths? | Scoring points after a try | *Changing a measurement into different units | A loft changed into a bedroom | A change of religion
exercise: «A loft conversion gave them an extra bedroom.» What does conversion mean in this sentence? | A new kind of roof made of glass | A kick at goal | *A loft changed for a new use | A cupboard for coats
test: «Christians speak of the conversion of Saint Paul.» What does conversion mean here? | A kick at goal after a try | Changing kilograms to grams | *A person changing their beliefs | Turning a barn into a home
test: Which phrase uses conversion to mean a building changed for a new use? | *Loft conversion | Energy conversion | Rugby conversion | Conversion tables
exam: Which word is the best clue that «a conversion adds 2» is about rugby? | *Try | Kilogram | Loft | Maths
Note: "Energy conversion" appears in the sense notes only; the test item above lists it as a distractor, which is correct because it is not a building.
